statement:
Let P, k ∈ ℕ, let U ⊆ ℝ^P be an arbitrary set, and let ω ∈ D^k(U) = TestFormOn U k (a C^∞ k-form on ℝ^P with compact support and tsupport ω ⊆ U). Let C₀, C₁ ⊆ ℝ^P be disjoint closed sets. Then there is ω′ ∈ D^k(U) such that:
(i) ω′(x) = 0 for all x in some open set N₀ ⊇ C₀;
(ii) ω′(x) = ω(x) for all x in some open set N₁ ⊇ C₁;
(iii) tsupport ω′ ⊆ tsupport ω;
(iv) |ω(x) − ω′(x)| ≤ |ω(x)| for every x ∈ ℝ^P.
Here |α| = covectorEuclideanNorm α is the Euclidean norm of the coefficients α(e_I), I strictly increasing.
